## Exp41 — Shared Discrete-Time Competing-Risk Survival Law — FULL PASS

### Frozen question

Can ONE TRAIN-fitted discrete-time competing-risk law generate coherent `15/30/60/120m` cumulative probabilities using only starting `CorridorPosition` and `Dwell`, instead of fitting separate Position/Dwell coefficients by horizon?

Frozen shared hazard laws:

```text
BASE_SURV:
  ADV vs STAY = alpha_ADV[k]
  REC vs STAY = alpha_REC[k]

POSITION_SURV:
  ADV vs STAY = alpha_ADV[k] + beta_ADV_geo * geo0
  REC vs STAY = alpha_REC[k] + beta_REC_geo * geo0

SEMI_SURV:
  ADV vs STAY = alpha_ADV[k] + beta_ADV_geo * geo0 + beta_ADV_dwell * dwell0
  REC vs STAY = alpha_REC[k] + beta_REC_geo * geo0 + beta_REC_dwell * dwell0
```

`k=1..24` future M5 steps; 24 nuisance elapsed-step intercepts per cause; Position/Dwell coefficients shared across all future steps. Starting covariates are frozen at `state_time`.

### Exact reproduction and coverage

All exact backbone guards passed before scoring. Exp40 eligible cells also reproduced exactly:

```text
TRAIN      21681 cells = 96.58%
VALIDATION  7577 cells = 96.69%
TEST        8008 cells = 95.52%
```

Per-horizon eligible counts also reproduced exactly:

```text
TRAIN      15m=5565 30m=5501 60m=5395 120m=5220
VALIDATION 15m=1942 30m=1919 60m=1885 120m=1831
TEST       15m=2076 30m=2046 60m=1988 120m=1898
```

TRAIN person-period table:

```text
67550 at-risk rows / 5612 starting states / 207 days
STAY=63795 | ADVANCE=1559 | RECAPTURE=2196
```

### Shared TRAIN coefficients

```text
POSITION_SURV
beta_ADV_geo = +0.48459159
beta_REC_geo = -0.46233758

SEMI_SURV
beta_ADV_geo   = +0.56488735
beta_ADV_dwell = -0.49064436
beta_REC_geo   = -0.38927814
beta_REC_dwell = -0.34241833
```

Thus Position keeps the expected oriented side geometry and starting Dwell reduces conditional future exit hazard for both causes after controlling for elapsed future step.

The TRAIN baseline conditional hazard also declines materially with future elapsed step. Example:

```text
  5m STAY=.899679 ADV=.038667 REC=.061654
 30m STAY=.942085 ADV=.024545 REC=.033370
 60m STAY=.957741 ADV=.016588 REC=.025671
120m STAY=.970199 ADV=.013907 REC=.015894
```

This is a hazard/survivorship pattern, not a causal claim.

