### Mechanistic diagnostics

Dwell again changes EXIT discrimination strongly while EXIT-side ranking is nearly unchanged.

TEST EXIT AUC delta from POSITION_SURV to SEMI_SURV:

```text
15m  +0.1096
30m  +0.1481
60m  +0.1391
120m +0.1256
```

TEST SIDE AUC deltas are approximately zero (`-0.0019/-0.0011/-0.0001/+0.0002`). This independently reinforces the existing factorization:

```text
CorridorPosition -> WHICH SIDE
Dwell            -> WHEN / WHETHER EXIT
```

Cumulative coherence is exact by construction in all splits:

```text
P(NO_EXIT) non-increasing = 100%
CIF_ADV non-decreasing    = 100%
CIF_REC non-decreasing    = 100%
probability sum error      ~= 1e-15
```

### Price of sharing vs Exp40 horizon-specific SEMI_H

Descriptive only; no rescue/non-inferiority claim.

```text
VALIDATION pooled price
Brier   +0.003328257
LogLoss +0.012416742

TEST pooled price
Brier   +0.002568691
LogLoss +0.015646675
```

The shared law loses only a small amount of Brier relative to four separately fitted horizon models and a modest amount of LogLoss. At TEST 120m, shared Brier was actually lower by `0.004026`, while shared LogLoss remained higher by `0.005364`. This isolated horizon observation is diagnostic only.

### Scientific interpretation

Exp41 materially strengthens the Track-D DNA. Exp40 showed multi-horizon predictive depth; Exp41 shows that most of that information can be represented by ONE coherent discrete-time competing-risk law with only shared Position/Dwell coefficients plus elapsed-step baseline hazards.

This is stronger evidence for a temporal state law than four unrelated horizon regressions, but it is still historical exploratory evidence because TEST has been repeatedly inspected. It is not a trading-rule backtest and does not authorize runtime promotion.

