# Exp42 — Directional Orientation Transport Stress Batch — FROZEN

Date frozen: 2026-08-13, after Exp41 completion and before any Exp42 subgroup score is inspected.

## Scientific question

The active-corridor representation orients price geometry by the current structural bias. Exp41 pooled `FULL_UP` and `FULL_DOWN` states after orientation. Exp42 asks whether the already-frozen Exp41 shared survival law transports on BOTH directional subpopulations without side-specific fitting.

This is a robustness/transportability stress test, not a new predictor search.

## Frozen model

Use the exact TRAIN-fitted Exp41 parameters unchanged:

```text
BASE_SURV
POSITION_SURV
SEMI_SURV
```

No side-specific refit, no `bias_sign` coefficient, no interaction, no recalibration.

## Frozen directional environments

Exactly two environments from starting `bias_sign`:

```text
FULL_UP   = bias_sign +1
FULL_DOWN = bias_sign -1
```

Use the same exact Exp41 eligible state-horizon cells and the same horizons `15/30/60/120m`.

## Estimand and uncertainty

Within each direction separately:

```text
PRIMARY = STATE_HORIZON_WEIGHTED pooled across all four horizons
UNCERTAINTY = whole-BRT-day bootstrap preserving all cells for that direction/day
```

Coverage gate: eligible cells / theoretical four-horizon cells for that direction must be >=70% in TRAIN, Validation and TEST.

## Frozen gates

Gate A — `POSITION_SURV vs BASE_SURV` must have Brier and LogLoss gain CI95 lower bound >0 in BOTH Validation and TEST for BOTH `FULL_UP` and `FULL_DOWN`.

Gate B — `SEMI_SURV vs POSITION_SURV` must satisfy the same 8-cell directional requirement.

Formal:

```text
DIRECTIONAL_POSITION_TRANSPORT = PASS only if Gate A passes both directions
DIRECTIONAL_DWELL_TRANSPORT = PASS only if Gate B passes both directions
ORIENTED_SHARED_SURVIVAL_LAW = PASS only if both gates pass
```

If any directional coverage is below 70%, formal status is `UNDERPOWERED_DIRECTIONAL_COVERAGE` rather than PASS/FAIL.

## Diagnostics only

- counts/states/days by direction and split;
- observed competing-risk distribution by direction/horizon;
- horizon-specific point gains by direction;
- EXIT/SIDE AUC by direction/horizon;
- directional calibration summaries;
- descriptive difference `FULL_UP minus FULL_DOWN` in score gains.

## Anti-rescue

```text
NO side-specific refit after result
NO bias_sign coefficient or interaction after result
NO separate UP/DOWN thresholds
NO horizon subset rescue
NO elapsed-step interaction rescue
NO new Position/Dwell transform
NO Exp38/39 coordinates
NO D1/Clock/Z/Fib/weekday/Scale/Energy/HMM context
NO Validation/TEST refit
NO Exp27 scoring/modification
```

If Exp42 fails while Exp41 remains strong, interpret that as: the pooled oriented shared survival law is valid historically, but exact UP/DOWN transport invariance is not established. Do not erase Exp41 and do not immediately rescue with side-specific models.

Historical OOS remains exploratory. Runtime promotion = NONE.
